prompt from `--prompt` or `--prompt-file`.\n2. Resolve and create `--out-dir`.\n3. Run the script from this skill.\n4. Inspect the returned JSON. Treat `success: true` and non-empty `images` as the completion signal.\n5. If the script fails, read `codex_output` and `error` in the JSON or terminal output before retrying with a clearer prompt.\n\n## Script\n\nMain script:\n\n```bash\nnode ~/.codex/skills/codex-image-gen/scripts/generate-image-with-codex.mjs --help\n```\n\nUseful options:\n\n- `--prompt <text>`: image prompt text.\n- `--prompt-file <path>`: read prompt from a file.\n- `--out-dir <dir>`: required output directory.\n- `--count <n>`: requested image count, default `1`.\n- `--prefix <name>`: preferred filename prefix, default `codex-image`.\n- `--model <model>`: pass a model to the child Codex command when using the default command.\n- `--codex-command <command>`: override the child command. Use this when the local CLI exposes a `codex -p \"prompt\"` style interface.\n- `--timeout-ms <n>`: child process timeout, default 10 minutes.\n- `--dry-run`: print the generated child prompt and command without running Codex.\n\nDefault child command:\n\n```bash\ncodex exec --skip-git-repo-check --sandbox danger-full-access -C <out-dir> <wrapped prompt>\n```\n\nIf the local Codex CLI uses `codex -p` for non-interactive prompting, run:\n\n```bash\nnode ~/.codex/skills/codex-image-gen/scripts/generate-image-with-codex.mjs \\\n  --prompt \"...\" \\\n  --out-dir ./imgs \\\n  --codex-command \"codex -p\"\n```\n\n## Prompt Guidance\n\nWrite prompts that include:\n\n- subject and scene\n- visual style\n- aspect ratio or orientation\n- text language and exact text, if text is required\n- output count\n- any brand or safety constraints\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n生成 1 张 16:9 横版中文技术知识卡。主题：/goal 如何让 Agent 持续工作到有证据。\n风格：奶油纸底 sketchnote，深海军蓝手绘线，低饱和便签色块。\n图片中文字保持简短中文标签，不要真实品牌 Logo。\n```\n\n## Failure Rules\n\nDo not silently create placeholder images when native Codex image generation 